\f0\b\fs32 \cf0 3. LAN vs. WAN\
\pard\pardeftab560\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\b0\fs18 \cf0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 LAN (Local Area Network):
\f1\b0  Your internal network (e.g., your home or office). It includes your computers, switches, and local traffic {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7MNX_UD7vY&t=89"}}{\fldrslt \uc0\u8232 }}.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f3\fs18 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}
\f0\b\fs26 WAN (Wide Area Network):
\f1\b0  The network that exists outside your home. The 
\f0\b Internet
\f1\b0  is essentially a massive WAN consisting of thousands of routers connected globally {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S7MNX_UD7vY&t=101"}}{\fldrslt \uc0\u8232 }}.\
\pard\pardeftab560\slleading20\partightenfactor0
